<body><main><a class="back" href="/lucas-capability-os-pages/legal-recruiter-lab/">← Recruiter Lab</a><p class="kicker">PRE-LAUNCH POLICY</p><h1>Privacy</h1><p class="lead">Recruiter Lab is designed to collect as little personal information as practical.</p><section><h2>What this site collects</h2><p>The current GitHub Pages learning demo has no account system, newsletter form, advertising tracker, or custom analytics implemented by Recruiter Lab. Standard hosting infrastructure may still process technical request data such as IP address, browser information, and timestamps.</p></section><section><h2>Purchases</h2><p>Checkout is handled by Lemon Squeezy. Information required for payment, tax, fraud prevention, receipts, and order fulfillment is processed through that platform under its own privacy and merchant-of-record obligations. Recruiter Lab should not request card numbers or identity documents directly from customers.</p></section><section><h2>Product access</h2><p>Digital files are delivered through the purchase platform. Order information may be used only as needed to provide the purchased product, respond to support requests, prevent abuse, and meet applicable recordkeeping obligations.</p></section><section><h2>Changes</h2><p>If Recruiter Lab later adds accounts, analytics, email marketing, community features, or other data collection, this notice must be updated before those features go live.</p></section><p class="note">Last updated: 8 September 2026. This pre-launch notice is operational information, not legal advice. Applicable privacy rights remain unaffected.</p><footer><a href="./terms">Terms</a><a href="./refund">Refunds</a><a href="./support">Support</a></footer><p class="flow">Flow note — This page documents the minimum-data boundary for the Recruiter Lab public surface and checkout flow.</p></main></body></html>
